            <ArticleTitle>Behavioural assessment and treatment of chronic headaches in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>359-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review explores advances in the behavioural assessment and treatment of childhood headaches. Behavioural assessment procedures are outlined including the behavioural interview, self-report questionnaires, self-monitoring and caregiver observations. We conclude that behavioural treatment strategies are effective in the management of childhood headaches, although most of the research support appears to be limited to relaxation training and biofeedback. Nonetheless, the behavioural assessment and treatment of childhood headaches appears to be a promising clinical and research direction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
